# CVE-2022-40152 (CWE-400/CWE-674): Woodstox's DTD reader recursed into
# nested content specifications with no depth limit, so a DOCTYPE whose
# <!ELEMENT> content spec nests a few thousand parentheses drove
# readContentSpec into a StackOverflowError and took the parsing thread
# down. readContentSpec in
# src/main/java/com/ctc/wstx/dtd/FullDTDReader.java walked the spec in a
# while(true) loop and, at every '(' token, called itself unconditionally
# -- `ContentSpec cs = readContentSpec(elemName, false, construct);` -- so
# nesting depth was bounded only by the input itself. The pool row carried
# nocommit; the flag is advisory-side absence only: 7e93907 ("add recursion
# limit of 500 for DTD parsing (#159)") is the fixing change, and it reads
# in full from the default clone -- the method gains a recursionDepth
# parameter, `if (recursionDepth > DTD_RECURSION_DEPTH_LIMIT) throw new
# XMLStreamException(...)` at entry, and the self-call passes
# `recursionDepth + 1`.
#
# ATTENTION, re-measured fresh on both revisions and both report views.
# Three `--cache off` runs per revision over src/main/java report one
# finding each, byte-identical: VYQL-NUM-014 on UTF8Writer.java:112, an
# offset-plus-length bounds heuristic in the writer, untouched by the fix.
# The `-flags only` view reports 36 flags per revision with identical
# sets; the only movement is the FullDTDReader ResourceRelease flag
# shifting 864 -> 885 with the twenty-one lines the fix adds above it.
# Nothing in either view names the content-spec walk.
#
# Extraction and resolution are not the blocker. `vyql graph` on the
# vulnerable FullDTDReader.java shows the self-call as a node
# (`Call path=readContentSpec` at :3090, inside fn377) with its arguments
# flowing into the enclosing function's own parameters
# (`Arg#3907 --FLOWS--> FullDTDReader.readContentSpec#param#elemName`),
# and `vyql resolve` counts 505 resolved call sites with readContentSpec
# absent from the unresolved list. The recursion is in the graph; no fact
# observes it.
#
# What stands, engine: presence predicates compare one field to a string
# literal (internal/bindings/compile_presence.go:229, re-verified on the
# current engine), so no predicate unifies node.context.functionName with
# node.context.callPath and "the callee is the enclosing function" does
# not compile -- the depth-budget family recorded for C (1320), JS (1391),
# Rust (1697), Scala (1586, 1776) and Kotlin (1954). The shipped
# JavaScript extglob binding states the same limit in its own comment:
# "`function_name:` and `call_path:` both reach it but no predicate can
# unify them".
#
# What stands, vocabulary: code.UnboundedResourceOperation (VYQL-DOS-042)
# has emitters in python, rust, javascript, swift and c, none in java, and
# each is anchored on its ecosystem's documented bounding vocabulary
# (asyncio's spawn and len() comparison, flate2's buffer-growth calls and
# min/clamp/take/truncate, python-multipart's window contract, RFC 8915's
# cookie exchange). The depth-limit concepts that do exist are
# per-ecosystem the same way: NestedExtglobExpansionWithoutDepthLimit
# (javascript, anchored on the documented `noext` option),
# NestedParamExpansionWithoutDepthLimit (ruby) and
# GsonObjectTypeAdapterRecursiveRead (java, keyed on Gson's own
# identifiers). Woodstox's readContentSpec is a private method with no
# public surface, so a binding naming it detects this parser rather than
# the weakness, and the fix's own spellings (recursionDepth,
# DTD_RECURSION_DEPTH_LIMIT) are the discriminator such a binding would
# key on.
#
# The discriminating fact is the budget asymmetry, the same shape the
# Kotlin sibling measured: woodstox documents and enforces two depth
# budgets at both revisions -- WstxInputProperties.P_MAX_ELEMENT_DEPTH
# ("com.ctc.wstx.maxElementDepth", default 1000) enforced in
# InputElementStack.java:326 as `if (++mDepth >
# mConfig.getMaxElementDepth()) throw ...`, and P_MAX_ENTITY_DEPTH
# ("com.ctc.wstx.maxEntityDepth") enforced in StreamScanner.java:976
# through verifyLimit("Maximum entity expansion depth", ...). The DTD
# content-spec walk consults neither budget at either revision; the fix
# adds its own static limit rather than routing through the config. So no
# fact naming the budget alone separates the revisions either -- only
# "the self-recursive call site consults a cap" does, which is the
# inexpressible half above.
#
# The one generic anchor available was measured and is not shippable: a
# function-scope `'('` character literal with a negation on generic depth
# identifiers (maxRecursion, recursionLimit, recursionDepth, maxDepth,
# depthLimit, maxNesting, nestingLimit, nestingDepth) reports 7 findings
# at the vulnerable revision and 6 at the fixed one. The six that persist
# are ChoiceContentSpec.java:123, ConcatModel.java:108 and
# SeqContentSpec.java:114 -- `sb.append('(')` in content-spec toString
# builders -- plus FullDTDReader's handleElementDecl, handleAttrDecl and
# readMixedSpec, three iterative walks that never recurse; only
# readContentSpec clears. Seven flagged for one true, six of them present
# at both revisions, and the anchor cannot name recursion at all. Its
# reach elsewhere is quiet on web code and wrong on parser code: zero
# `'('` character literals across the 2766-file OWASP Java benchmark
# corpus, one in the protobuf-java clone, twenty-eight over eighteen
# files in quarkus. (The protobuf-java scan itself stops at the --max-ram
# ceiling at 5.6 GiB resident, reported as measured rather than retried.)
#
# No definition change ships. Tests one and two hold the two revisions
# and both reject VYQL-DOS-029, VYQL-DOS-042 and VYQL-DOS-045: when
# recursion-depth budget vocabulary lands, the unbounded form must flip
# to expect.
#
# verify_current_expected: attention-engine-gap

test "rank1959: the content-spec walk recurses without a depth cap"
  lang java
  file src/main/java/com/ctc/wstx/dtd/FullDTDReader.java
  reject VYQL-DOS-029
  reject VYQL-DOS-042
  reject VYQL-DOS-045
  code
  ```
  package com.ctc.wstx.dtd;

  import java.util.ArrayList;
  import javax.xml.stream.XMLStreamException;

  class FullDTDReader
  {
      private ContentSpec readContentSpec(PrefixedName elemName, boolean mainLevel,
                                          boolean construct)
          throws XMLStreamException
      {
          ArrayList<ContentSpec> subSpecs = new ArrayList<ContentSpec>();
          boolean isChoice = false;
          boolean choiceSet = false;

          while (true) {
              char c = skipDtdWs(true);
              if (c == ')') {
                  if (subSpecs.isEmpty()) {
                      _reportWFCViolation("Empty content specification for '"+elemName+"' (need at least one entry)");
                  }
                  break;
              }
              if (c == '|' || c == ',') {
                  boolean newChoice = (c == '|');
                  if (!choiceSet) {
                      isChoice = newChoice;
                      choiceSet = true;
                  } else {
                      if (isChoice != newChoice) {
                          _reportWFCViolation("Can not mix content spec separators ('|' and ','); need to use parenthesis groups");
                      }
                  }
                  c = skipDtdWs(true);
              } else {
                  if (!subSpecs.isEmpty()) {
                      throwDTDUnexpectedChar(c, " (missing separator '|' or ','?)");
                  }
              }
              if (c == '(') {
                  ContentSpec cs = readContentSpec(elemName, false, construct);
                  subSpecs.add(cs);
                  continue;
              }
              PrefixedName thisName = readDTDQName(c);
              char arity = readArity();
              ContentSpec cs = construct ?
                  TokenContentSpec.construct(arity, thisName)
                  : TokenContentSpec.getDummySpec();
              subSpecs.add(cs);
          }

          char arity = readArity();
          if (subSpecs.size() == 1) {
              return subSpecs.get(0);
          }
          if (isChoice) {
              return ChoiceContentSpec.constructChoice(mCfgNsEnabled, arity, subSpecs);
          }
          return SeqContentSpec.construct(mCfgNsEnabled, arity, subSpecs);
      }
  }
  ```

test "rank1959: the fixed revision caps the content-spec recursion depth"
  lang java
  file src/main/java/com/ctc/wstx/dtd/FullDTDReader.java
  reject VYQL-DOS-029
  reject VYQL-DOS-042
  reject VYQL-DOS-045
  code
  ```
  package com.ctc.wstx.dtd;

  import java.util.ArrayList;
  import javax.xml.stream.XMLStreamException;

  class FullDTDReader
  {
      final static int DEFAULT_DTD_RECURSION_DEPTH_LIMIT = 500;
      static int DTD_RECURSION_DEPTH_LIMIT = DEFAULT_DTD_RECURSION_DEPTH_LIMIT;

      private ContentSpec readContentSpec(final PrefixedName elemName, final boolean construct,
                                          final int recursionDepth)
          throws XMLStreamException
      {
          if (recursionDepth > DTD_RECURSION_DEPTH_LIMIT) {
              throw new XMLStreamException("FullDTDReader has reached recursion depth limit of " + DTD_RECURSION_DEPTH_LIMIT);
          }

          ArrayList<ContentSpec> subSpecs = new ArrayList<ContentSpec>();
          boolean isChoice = false;
          boolean choiceSet = false;

          while (true) {
              char c = skipDtdWs(true);
              if (c == ')') {
                  if (subSpecs.isEmpty()) {
                      _reportWFCViolation("Empty content specification for '"+elemName+"' (need at least one entry)");
                  }
                  break;
              }
              if (c == '|' || c == ',') {
                  boolean newChoice = (c == '|');
                  if (!choiceSet) {
                      isChoice = newChoice;
                      choiceSet = true;
                  } else {
                      if (isChoice != newChoice) {
                          _reportWFCViolation("Can not mix content spec separators ('|' and ','); need to use parenthesis groups");
                      }
                  }
                  c = skipDtdWs(true);
              } else {
                  if (!subSpecs.isEmpty()) {
                      throwDTDUnexpectedChar(c, " (missing separator '|' or ','?)");
                  }
              }
              if (c == '(') {
                  ContentSpec cs = readContentSpec(elemName, construct, recursionDepth + 1);
                  subSpecs.add(cs);
                  continue;
              }
              PrefixedName thisName = readDTDQName(c);
              char arity = readArity();
              ContentSpec cs = construct ?
                  TokenContentSpec.construct(arity, thisName)
                  : TokenContentSpec.getDummySpec();
              subSpecs.add(cs);
          }

          char arity = readArity();
          if (subSpecs.size() == 1) {
              return subSpecs.get(0);
          }
          if (isChoice) {
              return ChoiceContentSpec.constructChoice(mCfgNsEnabled, arity, subSpecs);
          }
          return SeqContentSpec.construct(mCfgNsEnabled, arity, subSpecs);
      }
  }
  ```
